The desktop projection library (`libhuak_space.dylib` / `libhuak_space.so`)
statically links the OCCT 8.0.2 modeling toolkits (`V8_0_2`, commit
83f9abe9477af36e4ca218e1468068aed052779f) fetched via `build.zig.zon`. Huak
loads `libhuak_space` dynamically at runtime, so users can rebuild and replace
it against a modified OCCT build with `zig build space-backend`.

The optional local WASI build uses the OCCT 8.0.1 port and single-threaded
header from OCCTSwift (also LGPL 2.1). The kernel build, sources and patches
are identified at https://github.com/SecondMouseAU/OCCTSwift/tree/v4.0.0-kernel.8
